@startuml
title Verification & Account Flow - Email/Phone Verify + Cross-Channel Contact Change (M3)

actor Person

participant "VerifyPage" as VP
participant "ContactChangePage" as CP
participant "VerifyGateway" as VG
participant "AccountGateway" as AG
participant "ApiClient" as AC
participant "ApiInterceptor" as AI
participant "AuthStore" as AS
database "Spring Boot /verify + /account" as API

note over Person, API
  All endpoints below require a valid JWT (ApiInterceptor adds
  the Bearer token). Cooldown (60s) and daily cap (5) violations
  return 429 -> surface the uniform ErrorResponse message.
end note

== Verify a level (EMAIL first, then PHONE) ==
Person -> VP : "Verify my email" (post-register banner / /verify)
VP -> VG : request(EMAIL)
VG -> AC : post<void>('/verify/request', {level: EMAIL})
AC -> API : POST /verify/request
alt 202 Accepted
  API --> AC : (empty body)
  note over VP
    dev sender logs the code to the backend console;
    smtp-pulse delivers it to the inbox. PHONE does the same
    via DevSmsSender (console) or Twilio once credentials are set.
  end note
  VP --> Person : "enter the 6-char code / 6-digit OTP"
  Person -> VP : code
  VP -> VG : confirm(EMAIL, code)
  VG -> AC : post<void>('/verify/confirm', {level, code})
  AC -> API : POST /verify/confirm
  alt correct
    API --> AC : 200 (claim persisted)
    VP --> Person : verified - levels() includes EMAIL
  else wrong/expired (400) or throttled (429)
    API --> AC : ErrorResponse
    VP --> Person : retry with remaining attempts
  end
else 409 AlreadyVerified
  API --> AC : conflict
  VP --> Person : already verified - hide the button
else 429 throttled
  API --> AC : too many requests
  VP --> Person : wait and retry
end

note over VP
  Re-requesting an already-verified level -> 409 (M2 guard on the
  backend: no code is sent, no throttle consumed). Confirm is
  idempotent. UX: treat 409 on request as "you are verified".
end note

== Contact change: email -> phone SMS proof (cross-channel) ==
Person -> CP : "change email to new@example.com" (in /account)
CP -> AG : requestEmailChange(newEmail)
AG -> AC : post<void>('/account/email-change/request', body)
AC -> API : POST /account/email-change/request
note over API
  backend sends the OTP to the CURRENT PHONE (SMS), NOT to the
  new email - stealing the mailbox alone cannot change it.
end note
API --> AC : 202 Accepted
CP --> Person : "enter the SMS code sent to +372... "
Person -> CP : code
CP -> AG : confirmEmailChange(code)
AG -> AC : post<void>('/account/email-change/confirm', {code})
AC -> API : POST /account/email-change/confirm
API --> AC : 200 OK
CP --> Person : email updated
note over CP
  duplicate new email -> 409; same as current -> 400;
  sessions are NOT revoked by contact change (only a password
  reset revokes all refresh tokens).
end note

== Contact change: phone -> email code proof (cross-channel) ==
Person -> CP : "change phone to +3725..." (in /account)
CP -> AG : requestPhoneChange(newPhone)
AG -> AC : post<void>('/account/phone-change/request', body)
AC -> API : POST /account/phone-change/request
note over API
  backend sends the OTP to the CURRENT EMAIL - losing the SIM
  alone cannot let an attacker re-route verification texts.
end note
API --> AC : 202 Accepted
CP --> Person : "enter the code sent to current@email.com"
Person -> CP : code
CP -> AG : confirmPhoneChange(code)
AG -> AC : post<void>('/account/phone-change/confirm', {code})
AC -> API : POST /account/phone-change/confirm
API --> AC : 200 OK
CP --> Person : phone updated (E.164 normalized)

note over AS
  After any successful confirm the account page re-reads the
  profile so the UI shows the new contact immediately.
end note
@enduml
